## 🎯 SEARCH PACKAGE TESTING PHILOSOPHY [MANDATORY]

### 🚨 CRITICAL: Switch Statement Coverage [ZERO TOLERANCE]

**MANDATORY RULE**: For ANY class with switch statements (especially `NodeFactory`), you MUST achieve 100% branch coverage by testing EVERY case branch, including:
- ✅ Every `case` statement in every switch
- ✅ Every `default` case (exception paths)
- ✅ All conditional branches within switch cases

**Why Critical**: Switch statements are common sources of uncovered code. Missing a single case means incomplete coverage and potential bugs.

**Verification Process**:
1. Run coverage: `mvn clean test jacoco:report -Dtest="[TestClass]Tests"`
2. Open coverage report: `target/site/jacoco/index.html`
3. Check switch statements: Every case must show green (covered)
4. Check default cases: Every default must show green (covered)

**Common Mistakes to Avoid**:
- ❌ Testing only one or two cases from a switch statement
- ❌ Missing `default` case tests
- ❌ Assuming all cases are covered when only some are tested
- ❌ Not verifying coverage report after adding tests

**Before submitting any test code with switch statements, verify:**
- [ ] Every `case` branch is tested
- [ ] Every `default` branch is tested
- [ ] Coverage report shows 100% branch coverage for switch statements
- [ ] All exception paths are tested

### 1. Search Package Components Overview

The search package consists of:
- **Filter Nodes**: Individual filter implementations (e.g., `IsLessThanFilterNode`, `IsMoreThanFilterNode`)
- **AST Builder**: Builds abstract syntax tree from filter DTOs (`FilterSearchASTBuilder`)
- **Node Factory**: Creates filter nodes based on filter type and field (`NodeFactory`)
- **Constants**: Enums for filter types, date values, group types (`FilterTypes`, `DateIsFilterValue`, etc.)
- **Helpers**: Utility classes for date handling, field conditions, JOOQ field types (`DateHelper`, `FieldConditionSpecifications`, `JooqFieldTypeUtils`)
- **CTE Providers**: Common table expression providers for search queries (`TimesheetFilterSearchCteProvider`, `ContractorFilterSearchCteProvider`)

### 2. Filter Node Testing Strategy - MANDATORY APPROACH

#### 2.1 Filter Node Test Structure

**Filter nodes are pure logic classes that:**
- Parse filter values from `FilterDto`
- Generate JOOQ `Condition` objects based on filter logic
- Handle edge cases (null values, invalid formats, etc.)
- Apply GMT offset adjustments for date/time filters

**Test Pattern for Filter Nodes:**
```java
@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)
class [FilterNode]Tests {
    
    private FilterNodeContext filterNodeContext;
    private FilterDto filterDto;
    
    @BeforeEach
    void setUp() {
        this.filterDto = new FilterDto();
        this.filterNodeContext = new FilterNodeContext();
        this.filterNodeContext.setFilterDto(this.filterDto);
        this.filterNodeContext.setAccountId(1);
        this.filterNodeContext.setGmtDifference("+00:00");
    }
    
    @Test
    @DisplayName("Get filter conditions should return correct condition for valid filter value")
    void testGetFilterConditionsValidFilterValueReturnsCorrectCondition() {
        // Given
        this.filterDto.setFilterValue("10");
        IsLessThanFilterNode filterNode = new IsLessThanFilterNode(this.filterNodeContext);
        
        // When
        List<Condition> conditions = filterNode.getFilterConditions();
        
        // Then
        assertThat(conditions).isNotEmpty();
        assertThat(conditions.size()).isEqualTo(1);
    }
    
    @Test
    @DisplayName("Get filter conditions should return false condition for invalid filter value")
    void testGetFilterConditionsInvalidFilterValueReturnsFalseCondition() {
        // Given
        this.filterDto.setFilterValue("invalid");
        IsLessThanFilterNode filterNode = new IsLessThanFilterNode(this.filterNodeContext);
        
        // When
        List<Condition> conditions = filterNode.getFilterConditions();
        
        // Then
        assertThat(conditions).isNotEmpty();
        // Verify it returns falseCondition() for invalid input
    }
    
    @Test
    @DisplayName("Get filter conditions should handle null filter value")
    void testGetFilterConditionsNullFilterValueHandlesCorrectly() {
        // Given
        this.filterDto.setFilterValue(null);
        IsLessThanFilterNode filterNode = new IsLessThanFilterNode(this.filterNodeContext);
        
        // When
        List<Condition> conditions = filterNode.getFilterConditions();
        
        // Then
        assertThat(conditions).isNotEmpty();
        // Verify null handling
    }
    
    @Test
    @DisplayName("Is select distinct should return correct value")
    void testIsSelectDistinctReturnsCorrectValue() {
        // Given
        IsLessThanFilterNode filterNode = new IsLessThanFilterNode(this.filterNodeContext);
        
        // When
        Boolean isDistinct = filterNode.isSelectDistinct();
        
        // Then
        assertThat(isDistinct).isNotNull();
    }
}
```

