**🚨 AFTER WRITING TESTS - Verification Checklist:**
1. [ ] Run coverage report: `mvn clean test jacoco:report -Dtest="NodeFactoryTests"`
2. [ ] Open `target/site/jacoco/index.html` in browser
3. [ ] Navigate to `NodeFactory.java`
4. [ ] Verify ALL switch cases show green (covered) - **ZERO RED LINES**
5. [ ] Verify ALL default cases show green (covered)
6. [ ] Verify ALL exception paths show green (covered)
7. [ ] Verify ALL conditional branches show green (covered)
8. [ ] Verify 100% line coverage: All lines in NodeFactory must be executed
9. [ ] Verify 100% branch coverage: All switch cases and conditionals must be tested
10. [ ] If ANY red lines exist, add tests for those specific cases

**🚨 COMMON MISTAKES TO AVOID:**
- ❌ Testing only one or two cases from a switch statement
- ❌ Missing `default` case tests
- ❌ Missing field name variants (e.g., testing only `timesheetStatus` but not `timesheet_status`)
- ❌ Missing groupType routing paths (e.g., testing contractor path but not non-contractor path)
- ❌ Assuming all cases are covered when only some are tested
- ❌ Not verifying coverage report after adding tests
- ❌ Not reading the entire file before writing tests

**🚨 SYSTEMATIC APPROACH - Follow This Order:**
1. **Read `NodeFactory.java` completely** - identify ALL switch statements
2. **Create a checklist** - list every case for every switch statement
3. **Write tests systematically** - one test per case, following the pattern
4. **Run coverage** - verify 100% coverage
5. **Fix gaps** - add tests for any uncovered lines
6. **Re-verify** - run coverage again until 100% achieved

